{"term":"masquerade","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6164538de9b7616c1f","definition":"An assembly or party of people wearing (usually elaborate or fanciful) masks and costumes, and amusing themselves with dancing, conversation, or other diversions.","example":"Near-synonym: costume party","pos":"noun","synonyms":["masque","costume party"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive","register":"also, attributive","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b1670c489a92174b7c","definition":"The act of wearing a mask or dressing up in a costume for, or as if for, a masquerade ball.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive","register":"also, attributive","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dde4cebfdcbbd46d23","definition":"An act of living under false pretenses; a concealment of something by a false or unreal show; a disguise, a pretence; also, a pretentious display.","example":"Verres in the youth of Cicero, Catiline and Clodius in his middle age, Mark Antony in his old age, have all been left to operate on the modern reader's feelings precisely through that masquerade of misrepresentation which invariably accompanied the political eloquence of Rome.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive, figuratively","register":"also, attributive, figuratively","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e38fb5938ca37ef1b6","definition":"An assembly of varied, often fanciful, things.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive, figuratively","register":"also, attributive, figuratively","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8bb9f7f8ef070525f0","definition":"A cosplay event at which costumed attendees perform skits.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive, slang","register":"also, attributive, slang","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1fba24ce591c36267c","definition":"A dramatic performance by actors in masks; a mask or masque.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive, obsolete","register":"also, attributive, obsolete","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:350d88cbabc8694e24","definition":"A Spanish entertainment or military exercise in which squadrons of horses charge at each other, the riders fighting with bucklers and canes.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive, obsolete, rare","register":"also, attributive, obsolete, rare","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3297ed40c598b1d8e3","definition":"To take part in a masquerade; to assemble in masks and costumes; (loosely) to wear a disguise.","example":"I’m going to masquerade as an old-fashioned pilot. What are you going to dress up as?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive","register":"also, attributive, intransitive","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish","masqueradingly","masquerading","unmasqueraded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1be3351d2ed10bf786","definition":"To pass oneself off as a different person or a person with qualities that one does not possess; also, to make a pretentious show of being what one is not.","example":"He masqueraded as my friend until the truth finally came out.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive, figuratively","register":"also, attributive, figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish","masqueradingly","masquerading","unmasqueraded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f28cc7784483800a04","definition":"To appear as something else.","example":"A Foundation outpost masquerading as an abandoned home has been established within the vicinity of SCP-2003.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive, broadly, figuratively","register":"also, attributive, broadly, figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish","masqueradingly","masquerading","unmasqueraded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:294b277b63a1023bba","definition":"To conceal (someone) with, or as if with, a mask; to disguise.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, attributive, rare","register":"also, attributive, rare, transitive","wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish","masqueradingly","masquerading","unmasqueraded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masquerade#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˌmæskəˈɹeɪd/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/En-us-masquerade.mp3"},"wordFamily":["masquerader","masqueradish","masqueradingly","masquerading","unmasqueraded"]}